### USE CASE: 
Even if you try to change the property, it does not make any changes to your infrastructure.
For example:
You are creating an EC2 instance and you attempt to add a tag for billing-related operations for your company. However, you do not want Terraform to add new tags or modify existing tags.
By using lifecycle { ignore_changes = [tags] }, Terraform will ignore any changes made to the tags attribute in the configuration when you run terraform apply. As a result, Terraform will not update the tags on the existing EC2 instance, even if the code has been modified.

